# Monotone ratchet ceiling for `cargo xtask lint-no-free-port` (bd rc-d70up,
# mission 401; mirror of ratchet-test-sleep.max, bd rc-c9r6w).
#
# The integer below is the maximum allowed count of unadjudicated
# free-port probe definitions and call sites — identifiers matching
# `^(get_)?(free|find|prealloc|reserve|closed|unused|pick)_([a-z0-9_]+_)?port$`
# — across crates/, scripts/, examples/, benchmarks/, fuzz/. These
# helpers bind an ephemeral port, read it, and drop the listener before
# the real consumer binds (the ADR-0070 port-toctou class).
#
# Legitimacy rule: every residual site needs an
# `// allow-free-port: <reason>` marker on the line immediately above
# it; a definition marker does NOT cover its call sites, each site is
# adjudicated individually. Marked sites are suppressed at scan time and
# never count toward the ceiling. The number may only DECREASE — never
# raise it without review justification; the diff on this file is the
# regression signal.
#
# To lower it: fix sites (run `cargo xtask lint-no-free-port` — over a
# lowered ceiling it names every offender), then edit the number down
# to the new count and drop the fixed entries below.
#
# Seeded 2026-10-25 (mission 401) from the T1+T2 sweep recount: camel-test
# and camel-component-wasm are clean; the residual sites below are the
# out-of-scope crates tracked for future missions. Ceiling 17.
# Unadjudicated inventory at seed (2026-10-25), one entry per site —
